+# Drone MVP Medium Bag Sample Testing Completed (2026-10-28)
+
+## Summary
+
+On 2026-10-28 Jay relayed a follow-up from [[rob-knudson|Rob Knudson]] in the Slack thread that selected the Medium bag on 2026-08-12: IKC Ops has **completed the sample testing**. The mailed samples (the new August 2026 Medium bag, which the source describes as the PRD v26 default, together with the guest packaging) **fit the production Pod**. The **new Medium is confirmed as the MVP outer package**, and **no further bag testing is planned before launch**.
+
+This closes the "samples still need testing" condition carried since 2026-08-12 and turns Jay's 2026-08-20 interpretation (that the mailed samples were the new August Medium, not the current `10.5 × 10.5 × 12 in` Medium) from an inference into a stated fact of the source.
+
+It does not change the Zipline provider envelope (`338 × 254 × 205 mm / 2495 g`), does not publish a fill line, folded height, orientation or handle/closure rule, does not name the bag SKU or tare, and does not supply a written test report.
+
+## Detail
+
+### What the follow-up adds over the 2026-08-12 thread
+
+| Item | 2026-08-12 thread | 2026-10-28 follow-up |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Test object | 3D printed Pod sample | production Pod |
+| Bag tested | "existing Medium bag", SKU not pinned | new August 2026 Medium bag, stated to be the PRD v26 default |
+| Guest packaging | samples to be sent | tested together with the bag; fits |
+| Status | next step is to send samples for testing | testing complete; new Medium confirmed; no further bag testing before launch |
+
+### Effect on earlier conclusions
+
+- [[drone-mvp-medium-bag-outer-package-decision]] already stated (as of 2026-10-19, from PRD v26) that the new Medium is the default launch bag. This follow-up is independent corroboration from the IKC Ops / Rob channel rather than from the PRD, and it adds that physical sample testing against the production Pod is done.
+- The same Record's "Not Confirmed" list included separate Zipline test evidence. This follow-up asserts that the IKC Ops sample test is complete and passed; it still does not provide the test report, the tested configurations, or the fill/fold limits, so those items remain open.
+- The two-test-object distinction in that Record (IKC Pod-fit check with bags on hand versus mailed samples) is now partly resolved: the mailed samples are stated to be the new Medium and are what fit the production Pod.
+
+### Not resolved by this follow-up
+
+- **Which new-Medium dimensions were tested.** The source equates "the new August 2026 Medium bag" with "the PRD v26 default". [[drone-mvp-medium-bag-outer-package-decision]] records the August 2026 new Medium as `13 × 10 × 13 in` (paper twist handle) and the PRD v26 new Medium as `12 × 8.5 × 13 in`. Either these are the same bag described with two nominal tuples, or the source conflates two specs. The follow-up does not say, and this Record does not choose.
+- Bag SKU, empty-bag tare, maximum fill line, folded height, allowed orientation, handle/closure treatment.
+- A written Zipline or IKC Ops test report; the evidence here is a relayed Slack message (Jay relaying Rob relaying IKC Ops), recorded as text because the screenshot was not retained.
+- Whether "no further bag testing before launch" is an IKC Ops statement or Rob's summary of it.
+
